  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int_{1}^{5}[|x-3|+|1-x|] d x$\r\n$=\\int_{1}^{5}|x-3| d x+\\int_{1}^{5}|1-x| d x$\r\n$=\\int_{1}^{3}|x-3| d x+\\int_{3}^{5}|x-3| d x+\\int_{1}^{5}|1-x| d x$\r\n$=\\int_{1}^{3}-(x-3) d x+\\int_{3}^{5}(x-3) d x$\r\n$+\\int_{1}^{5}-(1-x) d x$\r\n$=\\int_{1}^{3}(3-x) d x+\\int_{3}^{5}(x-3) d x+\\int_{1}^{5}(x-1) d x$\r\n$=\\left[3 x-\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right]^{3}+\\left[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}-3 x\\right]_{3}^{5}+\\left[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}-x\\right]_{0}^{5}$\r\n$=\\left(3 \\times 3-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)-\\left(3 \\times 1-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{5 \\times 5}{2}-3 \\times 5\\right)$\r\n$\\begin{aligned}-\\left(\\frac{3 \\times 3}{2}-3 \\times 3\\right)+\\left(\\frac{5 \\times 5}{2}-5\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-1\\right) \\\\=\\left(9-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)-\\left(3-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{25}{2}-15\\right)-\\left(\\frac{9}{2}-9\\right) \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{25}{2}-5\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\=& \\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\=& \\frac{9-5-5+9+15+1}{2}=\\frac{24}{2}=12 \\end{aligned}$"
  }
